{
 "schema": "revised-phase-baseline/1",
 "status": "SMOKE instance for the MICHAEL cohort — an instrument test, NOT a scientific result.",
 "notes": [
  "One microphone, one held-out window per regime, two frozen render seeds, and family",
  "selection switched off (the declared family is used directly) so the run exercises the",
  "Michael gate wiring — the FLY124 MAE-ratio gate plus the conditional composite and",
  "absolute-LTAS non-regression gates and their block-level tolerances — without paying for",
  "the 16-window family comparison. The 'candidate' arm is the RAW-era FLY125 cruise export",
  "used as a stand-in so --check has something real to measure; it is not a revised candidate",
  "and consumes no candidate round."
 ],
 "scorer": {"experiment": "hppnet_l2_r2_s0", "ckpt": "best"},
